<p>The UK Parliament has approved the Tobacco and Vapes Bill, clearing the way for a law that will permanently bar anyone born on or after January 1, 2009 from legally buying tobacco products. The policy works by raising the legal age for buying tobacco by one year, every year, starting in 2027, so today’s younger generation will never become legally eligible to buy cigarettes under the system. Ministers say the measure is meant to create the UK’s first “smoke-free generation” and reduce deaths, disability, and ill health linked to smoking, which coverage describes as one of the country’s leading causes of preventable harm. The bill is expected to become law after royal assent. It also gives ministers new powers to regulate vaping and other nicotine products, including packaging and flavours, as the government tries to curb youth uptake while protecting public health.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/TfEugkZyf-NuNa5IGN0OgRgbQE_8wV8xLbVSYZG5kp5ccw4lDsoQ9IUCBrjO3BV3OSOk53pyMgGL2yitkEWh6WnsgHy_cYePA8tAiOKFLNABAI5GRcbgGE9gzAk0z6Ui5cH9GBtPKo208Pdt3-SIHYmZNokHoM-CXmPx9wGn-bpq475a00l2WeCNUZa1q9ZezhSlEkjakufK4Q' alt='The proposed lifetime smoking ban will apply in England, Scotland, Wales and Northern Ireland.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Royal assent: Reports said the bill had cleared Parliament and was expected to receive royal assent before becoming law.</li><li>Products covered: The lifelong sales ban applies more broadly to tobacco products under the legislation, according to multiple outlets.</li><li>Age threshold: The cutoff means people who are now 17 or younger fall under the future ban, while those already old enough to buy tobacco can still do so legally.</li><li>Policy origins: The bill’s path through Parliament began on November 5, 2024 and ended after the House of Lords approved amendments made by MPs.</li></ul><blockquote>Historic moment for the nation&#x27;s health - Wes Streeting</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Wes Streeting: The UK health minister said the measure would help create the country’s first smoke-free generation and protect young people from addiction and harm. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3350946/uk-agrees-ban-cigarette-sales-people-born-after-2008'>SCMP</a>)</li><li>UK government ministers: Ministers framed the bill as a way to save lives and, over time, ease pressure on the National Health Service by reducing smoking-related disease. (<a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-04-21-0700/public-health-bill-banning-people-born-after-2008-buying-tobacco-clears-uk-parliament'>AllSides</a>)</li><li>Policy coverage in Al Jazeera: Coverage highlighted how the law works in practice: instead of a one-time jump in the legal age, the purchase age will rise each year so the affected group never ages into eligibility. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2026/4/22/uk-bans-a-generation-of-children-from-smoking-how-it-works'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2026/4/22/uk-bans-a-generation-of-children-from-smoking-how-it-works'>UK bans a generation of children from smoking: How it works</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3350946/uk-agrees-ban-cigarette-sales-people-born-after-2008'>UK agrees ban on cigarette sales for people born after 2008</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/uk-agrees-ban-on-cigarette-sales-for-people-born-after-2008/article70891529.ece'>U.K. agrees ban on cigarette sales for people born after 2008</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/born-after-2008-you-may-never-legally-smoke-in-the-uk-with-new-tobacco-law-11392688#publisher=newsstand'>Born After 2008? You May Never Legally Smoke In The UK With New Tobacco Law</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/21/world/europe/uk-smoking-ban-2009.html'>Proposed Lifetime Smoking Ban to Become Law in Britain</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/uk-lawmakers-approve-lifetime-smoking-ban-for-todays-under-18s'>UK lawmakers approve lifetime smoking ban for today&#x27;s under-18s</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-04-21-0700/public-health-uk-permanently-ban-future-generations-buying-cigarettes-it-will-save-lives'>UK to permanently ban future generations from buying cigarettes: &#x27;It will save lives&#x27;</a> - allsides.com</li></ul>